<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Schweitzer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1875–1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Schweitzer was an Alsatian theologian, organist and physician, born at Kaysersberg in 1875. In 1913 he founded a hospital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lambarene">Lambaréné</a> in Gabon, then a French colony, where he worked for most of the rest of his life. His philosophy of 'reverence for life' earned him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> for 1952.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-schweitzer.jpg" alt="Albert Schweitzer" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-D0116-0041-019,_Albert_Schweitzer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
